    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "No, I just what I had was one short question for Congressman Rokana and that is I wanted to ask you, Congressman, if you've had the chance to review the hearings and, you know, the testimony that was given and entered into the record by a chairperson, Jerry Connelly from Virginia, Alexandria Costello Cortez, that was talking about, you know, having an honest national conversation about poverty and the truth about poverty, and who is the fact that there's a lot of people that are being left out of getting any jobs period, and the several testimonies were given, one by Kate Hutchinson, from West Virginia. And I was wondering if you've had the chance to review any of that. And second part of this question is to remember to be inclusive of those who don't have jobs or who can't get jobs or who are disabled for also getting a UBI because it's kind of important when you need money to be able to live. And it seems to me to be unconscionable that we don't condemn convicted experts to start to death or to die Allen Street from homelessness and poverty. But we do that to people who just weren't lucky in life and ended up sinking in further and further in poverty, no matter how hard they tried, against oftentimes incredible adversity and barriers to entry to jobs. and that's my question and I hope I",
