    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "I do think that's why I have the bill with Tim Ryan at $2,000 a month. I think in a low interest rate, low inflation environment, you can't. Now, obviously, I think at some point over the next 10 years, you probably will have inflationary pressure, which means that we have to be increasing the minimum wage. If costs are going to go up by, let's say, 70% over the next 10 years, which most economics at some point at will, then you need to be increasing minimum wage. But the most economists would say that there is no problem with printing money until you get to inflation. And right now, we have a low inflation, low interest rate environment, which is why I think we should be supporting every American with $2,000.",
