  {
    "episode_id": 84135,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84135.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 83,
    "turn_text": "Yes, I'm interested in the yes, you suggested that there could be quite a number of tech jobs that people could go into for an income however that the retraining people for tech jobs is relatively ineffective that only works for a small proportion of the population and not everyone will have the necessary skills or ability to to be trained in that era. And the tech industry, I happen to know because I'm actually a management consultant in the tech strategy company. A lot of companies are planning to automate their workforce. And a lot of workers in the tech industry are concerned that they will lose their jobs. And even if you retrain a number of the population, is not going to be enough jobs for them how would you resolve this",
