    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84135.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 87,
    "turn_text": "I think some of them are basic jobs of robotics process automation. So that's creating all these bots that are doing things to process it, businesses, automated businesses, but they still need someone who's actually creating them. And this turns out the skill of that only takes three to six months of training or understanding basic design. software design or understanding basic tech support, Salesforce becoming a Salesforce technician or understanding Amazon Web Services and the cloud and how to operate that. All of the businesses, some of the businesses are digitally operated. They're basically digital platforms of the modern factories of the 21st century are creating apps. So there are a lot of jobs I think for the next generation that can be done and that can be a core base within communities. But I want to make clear that we also need investment in roads and bridges and water systems and the electric grid and clean tech. And I don't think we can just create a nation of tech support or coders. I mean, that's unrealistic. What we need to do though is understand the innovation economy is a huge creator of jobs and wealth, and it should be more shared.",
