        "text": "Policymakers should move beyond GDP and focus on enabling meaningful lives and pursuit of happiness.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The capabilities approach challenges the notion that GDP alone should define economic success.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The capabilities approach and human development were introduced in the 1990s.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Capabilities include the ability to have family, health, and recreation.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "These capabilities are considered true measures of societal and individual well-being.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Martha Nussbaum is a famous philosopher.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Gene Spiring served as an economic advisor in both the Obama and Clinton administrations.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Martha Essen is a Nobel Laureate economist.",
