    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 84135,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84135.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 100,
    "turn_text": "Hi, Representative Kana. So David came actually wanted to be here today to talk with you, but he actually had to go back to work part-time because campaigning is expensive and it's difficult to run if you don't already have money, right? So this really highlights the issue of who is able to run for office. So the district that he's running to represent is the 10th poorest in the nation where some neighborhoods have a median income as low as $12,000 a year. So what kind of policy proposals and reforms do you think can help people from that district run for office to be able to advocate for themselves and the communities?",
