    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84135.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 112,
    "turn_text": "Hello. Hello. Thank you. So first of all, I just wanted to go back to Jacqueline's question that you responded to because really she was asking about the people who are falling through the existing safety net as it is currently structured. And Jacqueline knows firsthand how big those holes are and You responded with the typical programs of minimum wage, EITC, and amplifying or increasing the disability programs. So I just want to emphasize too that right now, and I'm hopefully you're aware of this, but 13 million people in poverty right now receives zero dollars from the federal government. And if you have a disability, about four out of five people with a disability right now in this country, get nothing, they don't qualify for disability. And disability, the program itself qualifying for it, people can wait two years, and a million people right now are waiting two years to actually qualify as being sufficiently disabled in order to receive assistance. The EITC program only reaches three out of four people who qualify for that program. Minimum wage, of course, does not help people who have disabilities who are unable to work in the system and EITC would also ignore them because EITC has a ramp up so that it gives nothing to those not earning enough. So I just wanted to emphasize that there are big holes there that I think we need to come to terms with and I think UBI is important for that because it actually reaches 10 out of 10 people instead of fractions of those people. Now, my question is actually the same as that I asked him when he was with us. And that question is, do you think there is someone in the GOP who is potentially more likely than others to co-sponsor your bill? I was really encouraged by say the recent bipartisan bill put forth by Justin Amash and Anna Presley. And I'm hoping that we can get someone from GOP to co-sponsor your bill. And I'm hoping if we can apply pressure to anyone, do you think that there's someone out there that is on the edge or something of co-sponsoring that you think might be able to do it?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_08",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Currently, 13 million people living in poverty receive no federal financial support.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Jacqueline is personally familiar with gaps in the current safety net.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Universal Basic Income (UBI) would reach every individual, unlike targeted programs which serve only partial populations.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Approximately 4 out of 5 people with disabilities in the U.S. do not receive any disability benefits.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "People applying for disability benefits often face a two-year wait before qualification.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The respondent addressed Jacqueline’s question using standard policy solutions: minimum wage, EITC, and expanded disability programs.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "About one million people are currently awaiting approval for disability benefits after a two-year delay.",
